candidates.reviewSummary:
I approve this diff: I found no reason to reject it.

**Same diff:** the diff is the staged change in /home/user/hackathon/.claude/worktrees/wf_cef6ac63-cc8-1. All 14 before/after file hashes match the proposal. I exported it to /tmp/loop-review-2-close/proposal.diff, and `git apply --check` passes cleanly on HEAD (d2151ed) in /tmp/loop-review-2-close/wt.

**Tests and typecheck:** `npm test` passes 214/214, against 191 at base. The 23 new tests are 6 in core tree.test.ts, 10 in swarm close.test.ts and 7 in lab arena-close.test.ts. `tsc -b --force` exits 0. No existing test is edited or deleted; tree.test.ts only gains tests. It does not touch arena.ts, arena-cli.ts, loop-judge.mjs or worktree-setup.sh.

**Bit-identical claim:** confirmed. `arena-cli eval` output files are byte-identical between base and the proposal on seeds 801–1000 and 5600–5749 (all 350 research worlds).

**Cut-rung numbers:** reproduced independently. Dropping the cut rung gives +0.048pp [90% −0.064, +0.160] on seeds 801–1000 and +0.120pp [−0.029, +0.269] on 5600–5749. The cut fires 9.14 times per world on 801–900. The pre-loop-1 fixed ladder (f5b2d80) gives 18.49. The cut rung stays on, so this is a structure proposal and utility does not drop.

**Point-in-time:** the new `onTick` seam runs at the start of tick t and receives only t and the live tree. `close()` and `applyTargets` read only current tree state. Skill is not identified by strategy class. The seed-specific numbers appear only in docs, comments and test fixtures (arena seeds 1–6, a seed-7 market with a scripted GOLD path). The mechanism itself contains none.

**Do the tests prove the guarantees?** Yes. I ran 16 mutants against the new tests, and every one made them fail:
- stop-out put back to "resize to 0, then revoke";
- stop-out as a bare revoke;
- start audit removed; end audit removed;
- delegate's revoked-ancestor check removed;
- NOT_CLOSED, STOP_NOT_REVOKED, LIVE_BUT_REVOKED and ROOT_CHANGED checks each removed;
- core audit removed from bookViolations;
- sub-mandates no longer grow back with their agent;
- grows no longer clipped to what the parent has;
- ppm-sum check removed;
- `capitalOf` still counting a closed agent's budget as capital;
- `isClosed` returning true for any revoked node;
- `isClosed` ignoring the revoked flag (a live subtree with no unspent authority counts as closed).

**Fuzz run:** I also ran 240 extra books: 40 arena worlds × deploy 0.8/0.995 × three policies, with random sub-mandate shares and random desk spending. They produced 0 exceptions, 0 refused moves and a clean audit at the end. The API itself rejects negative budgets, as DESIGN.md claims. The only failures were at deploy 1.0: that setting already fails at base because of setup rounding.

The problems list has four minor non-blocking notes. Scratch files are in /tmp/loop-review-2-close/: worktrees `wt` and `base`, `proposal.diff`, the eval output JSONs and `mutate.mjs`.
